    ferieSideSatser:'Holiday pay rates',
    ferieSideWhat:'What is holiday pay?',
    ferieSideWhatBody:'Holiday pay is statutory under the Holiday Act (Ferieloven) § 10. The employer cannot give less than 10,2 %, but collective agreements may give more (typically 12 % for 5 weeks\' holiday). It is normally paid out in June the year after it is earned and is taxable income, even though no tax is withheld at the time of payment.',
    kalkDekningsbidragSideWhat:'What is contribution margin?',
    kalkDekningsbidragSideWhatBody:'Contribution margin (CM) is the selling price minus the variable cost per unit — what is left to cover fixed costs and provide a profit. Break-even is the number of units you must sell before the total CM covers all fixed costs.',
    likvidSideWhat:'What is a liquidity budget?',
    likvidSideWhatBody:'An overview of your cash flow month by month — not the accounting profit. Opening balance plus income minus expenses, accumulated. It shows early on which months you may run out of money and need reserves.',
    bvlSideWhat:'Buy or rent?',
    bvlSideWhatBody:'Over short horizons, buying often loses out — transaction costs (document duty + estate agent fee on sale) eat up the gain. Over 15–20 years buying almost always wins, because the increase in value and the build-up of wealth through instalments accumulate. The figures here include a 22 % tax deduction on interest.',
    dokSideAvgifter:'Charges on purchase',
    dokSideMethod:'How we calculate',
    avsSideSaldo:'Declining-balance groups 2026',
    avsSideMethod:'Declining-balance or straight-line?',
    avsMethod1B:'Declining-balance depreciation',
    avsMethod1:'is the main rule for tax — a fixed percentage of the remaining value each year.',
    avsMethod2B:'Straight-line depreciation',
    avsMethod2:'is used in the accounts when the useful life is known — equal amounts each year.',
    avsMethod3:'An asset above 30 000 kr with an expected useful life of more than 3 years',
    avsMethod3B:'must be capitalised and depreciated',
    avsMethod4B:'Improvements (capital expenditure)',
    avsMethod4:'are added to the balance; sale/scrapping is deducted. A negative balance gives a gain.',
    avsMethod5:'The maximum rate is optional — you can depreciate at a lower rate if you have little profit.',
