    bvlHowtoRows: [['— HOW TO USE THE CALCULATOR —','Compare total cost of owning vs renting over time'],['Purchase price','What the home costs to buy. Plus equity = home budget.'],['Equity','Share you pay yourself. The Lending Regulation requires min 10%.'],['Mortgage rate','Average rate over the loan period. Use today\'s rate if unsure.'],['Monthly rent','What a comparable home would cost to rent today.'],['Common costs','Monthly condo/HOA fees. Apartments typically 2,000-5,000 kr/month.'],['Maintenance','Annual upkeep as share of home value. Typically 1% (Norwegian standard).'],['Time horizon','How long will you live there? Shorter = renting often better. Longer = owning often better.'],['House-price growth','Expected annual growth. Norwegian historic average 1990-2024 is ~5%/year, but fluctuates.'],['Rent growth','Expected rent growth. Often 2-4%/year in big cities.'],['Alt. return','What your equity would earn in funds if you rented. Index funds average ~6-7%/year.'],['— HOW TO READ THE RESULTS —',''],['Total cost — buying','Interest + common costs + maintenance − tax deduction − value growth (net).'],['Total cost — renting','Accumulated rent over the period − alternative return on equity.'],['Break-even','Roughly when owning becomes cheaper than renting.'],['Equity built by owning','Home value − remaining loan. What you\'re left with.'],['— GOOD TO KNOW —',''],['Short horizon','If you move within 5 years, owning often loses — transaction costs (2.5% stamp duty + agent on sale) eat the gain.'],['Long horizon','Over 15-20 years owning almost always wins due to value growth + equity accumulation.'],['Uncertain rate','Run the calculator with different rates — see how much it affects the result.']],
