    financeHeroTitle: 'Financial calculator',
    financeHeroLead: 'Calculate present value (PV), future value (FV), margin/markup, break-even, compound interest and discounts. Pick a calculation type, fill in the numbers and get the result with details. Everything runs locally in your browser.',
    financeSectionInput: 'Financial calculation',
    financeSectionHint: '5 types',
    financeInfoBox: 'The financial calculator covers five typical calculations: present/future value (TVM), margin and markup, break-even, compound interest and discounts. Results update locally — no data leaves your device.',
    renteTitle: 'Effective rate',
    renteSubtitle: 'Calculate the real annual rate on your loan — not just what the bank advertises. Includes origination fee and monthly fees. Compare actual loan costs. Everything happens locally in your browser.',
    renteSectionInput: 'Loan details',
    renteSectionHint: 'Annuity loan',
    renteStatEff: 'Effective annual rate',
    renteStatTotal: 'Total cost',
    renteBtnCalc: 'Calculate effective rate',
    renteRVerdict: 'Enter loan amount and rate to see the calculation',
    renteVerdictAbove: 'Effective rate is {diff} percentage points higher than nominal — fees cost you extra.',
    renteVerdictEqual: 'Effective rate is practically equal to nominal — minimal fees.',
    renteHowtoTitle: 'How to use the Effective Rate calculator',
    renteHowtoLead: 'The effective rate is the actual cost of the loan — not just the nominal rate the bank advertises. It includes all fees and charges.',
    renteHowtoP1: '<strong>Loan amount</strong> is what you borrow. <strong>Nominal rate</strong> is what the bank quotes, before fees.',
    renteHowtoP2: '<strong>Origination fee</strong> is deducted from the loan at disbursement — you receive less than you borrow. <strong>Monthly fee</strong> is added to the rate each month.',
    renteHowtoP3: 'The effective rate is solved numerically: we find the annual rate where the present value of all payments (incl. monthly fee) equals the net disbursement (loan − origination fee).',
    renteHowtoP4: 'Always compare loans on effective rate, not nominal. A loan with a 4% nominal rate and high fees can cost more than 5% with no fees.',
