    regnskapMvaResNetPay: 'VAT payable',
    regnskapMvaResNetRefund: 'VAT refundable',
    regnskapMvaWhatTitle: 'What is the VAT return?',
    regnskapMvaWhatBody: 'The VAT return (form RF-0002) is submitted to the Tax Authority every 2 months. It shows how much VAT the business has collected from customers (output VAT) and how much it has paid on its own purchases (input VAT). The difference is the VAT payable or refundable.',
    regnskapMvaFristTitle: 'When is the VAT return due?',
    regnskapMvaFristBody: 'The deadline is 1 month + 10 days after the end of the period. Example: 1st period (Jan–Feb) has a deadline of 10 April. Businesses with turnover under 50 000 kr per 12 months are exempt from registration.',
    regnskapMvaSatsTitle: 'Which rate applies?',
    regnskapMvaSatsBody: '25 % is the standard rate for most goods and services. 15 % applies to food and beverages in grocery stores. 12 % is used for passenger transport, lodging, cinema tickets and museums. 0 % applies to exports, newspapers and books — but you can still claim a deduction for input VAT on these.',
    regnskapMvaRefundTitle: 'Refund or payment?',
    regnskapMvaRefundBody: 'If you have purchased more (input VAT) than you have sold (output VAT) in the period — typically during start-up or major investments — the Tax Authority refunds the difference to you.',
