    kalkFoodcostResInkl: 'Menu price incl. VAT',
    kalkFoodcostSectionTitle: 'Dish and price',
    kalkFoodcostSectionHint: 'Ingredient cost + one of: menu price or food cost',
    kalkFoodcostLblKost: 'Ingredient cost per dish',
    kalkFoodcostModeLbl: 'I want to enter',
    kalkFoodcostModeFc: 'Target food cost %',
    kalkFoodcostModeMeny: 'Menu price',
    kalkFoodcostValLblFc: 'Target food cost',
    kalkFoodcostValHintFc: 'Typically 28–35 % for hot dishes in a restaurant.',
    kalkFoodcostValLblMeny: 'Menu price incl. VAT',
    kalkFoodcostValHintMeny: 'The price the guest pays — we work out the food cost from it.',
    kalkFoodcostMvaLbl: 'VAT rate',
    kalkFoodcostMva25: '25 % · dining in',
    kalkFoodcostMva15: '15 % · take away / catering',
    kalkFoodcostResHeadline: 'Result',
    kalkFoodcostResFaktor: 'Price factor',
    kalkFoodcostResRund: 'Rounded menu price',
    kalkFoodcostNote: 'The calculation is done excl. VAT. The guest\'s menu price is shown incl. VAT — feel free to round up to a neat price.',
    kalkFoodcostFormelToggle: 'Show formula',
    kalkFoodcostF1: 'Food cost (%) = Ingredient cost / Selling price × 100',
    kalkFoodcostF2: 'Selling price excl. VAT = Ingredient cost / target food cost%',
    kalkFoodcostF3: 'Menu price incl. VAT = Selling price excl. VAT × (1 + VAT)',
    kalkFoodcostF4: 'Contribution margin = Selling price excl. VAT − Ingredient cost',
    kalkFoodcostF5: 'Price factor = 1 / target food cost%',
    kalkFoodcostFNote: '“A low food cost means a higher margin per dish — but the price also has to be right for the guest. 28–35 % is normal.”',
    kalkFoodcostGuideKicker: 'How to calculate',
    kalkFoodcostGuideTitle: 'From ingredient cost to menu price',
    kalkFoodcostStep1: '<b>Work out the ingredient cost per dish.</b> Add up the cost of every ingredient in the portion — excl. VAT.',
    kalkFoodcostStep2: '<b>Choose your target food cost.</b> 28–35 % is normal in a restaurant. Divide the ingredient cost by the food cost share to get the selling price excl. VAT.',
    kalkFoodcostStep3: '<b>Add VAT and round off.</b> 25 % for dining in, 15 % for take away. Round up to a neat menu price for the guest.',
    kalkFoodcostTableTitle: 'The example step by step',
    kalkFoodcostColSteg: 'Step',
    kalkFoodcostT1: 'Ingredient cost / food cost%',
    kalkFoodcostT2: 'Selling price − ingredient cost',
    kalkFoodcostT3Lbl: 'Dining in (25 % VAT)',
    kalkFoodcostT3: '73.33 × 1.25',
    kalkFoodcostT4Lbl: 'Take away (15 % VAT)',
    kalkFoodcostT4: '73.33 × 1.15',
    kalkFoodcostTableNote: '73.33 kr excl. VAT becomes 91.67 kr with the dining-in VAT rate — round to 92–95 kr on the menu. The price factor of 3.33 is a quick rule of thumb: multiply the ingredient cost by 3.33 for a 30 % food cost.',
    kalkFoodcostWhoKicker: 'Who uses it',
    kalkFoodcostWhoTitle: 'Three typical cases',
    kalkFoodcostWho1Lbl: 'Café · dish of the day',
    kalkFoodcostWho1Desc: 'Ingredient cost 22 kr, target 30 %. Menu price 92 kr incl. dining-in VAT.',
    kalkFoodcostWho2Lbl: 'Restaurant · à la carte',
    kalkFoodcostWho2Desc: 'A higher ingredient cost calls for a lower food cost target — 28 % leaves more room for wages and waste.',
    kalkFoodcostWho3Lbl: 'Catering · take away',
    kalkFoodcostWho3Desc: '15 % VAT on food taken off the premises — same calculation, lower price for the guest.',
    kalkFoodcostFaqQ1: 'What is a good food cost?',
    kalkFoodcostFaqA1: '28–35 % is normal for hot dishes in a restaurant. Drinks are often lower. A low food cost gives more contribution margin per dish, but the price still has to feel right to the guest.',
    kalkFoodcostFaqQ2: 'Which VAT rate applies?',
    kalkFoodcostFaqA2: 'Dining in carries 25 % VAT. Food sold to be taken away (take away and catering) counts as foodstuffs and carries 15 %. So the same dish can have two prices.',
    kalkFoodcostFaqQ3: 'What is the price factor?',
    kalkFoodcostFaqA3: 'The number you multiply the ingredient cost by to hit your target: 1 divided by the food cost share. A 30 % food cost gives a factor of 3.33 — quick mental arithmetic when you price new dishes.',
    kalkFoodcostRel1Desc: 'Set the right price from the cost of goods, and see the difference between markup and the contribution margin ratio.',
    kalkFoodcostRel2Desc: 'Full costing from materials to price, with overhead add-ons and profit.',
    kalkFoodcostRel3Desc: 'Cost per unit — even when the variants use different amounts of resources.',
    kalkLandedcostTitle: 'Landed cost',
    kalkLandedcostSubtitle: 'What the goods actually cost you once landed — freight, customs duty and fees included.',
    kalkLandedcostStatLanded: 'Landed cost in the example',
    kalkLandedcostStatFrakt: 'Freight per unit',
